WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.495
Voyager 1, and everything behind it.

00:03.227 --> 00:14.394
It passed Jupiter in March 1979 and Saturn in November 1980, and it has been leaving ever since, more than 170 times the Earth's distance from the Sun.

00:14.897 --> 00:19.072
In 1990 it turned round and photographed the planets it had left.

00:19.689 --> 00:23.022
Earth came out 0.12 of a pixel wide.
